WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:04.200
When Donald Trump ran for President

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.320
he promised to institute a 100 day action plan to make America great again.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.260
As the 100 day mark approaches, how is he
doing?

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.940
Reason presents the 3 worst and the 3 best achievements

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:17.600
of President Trump's first 100 days.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.740
Bing bing bing!

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.900
We will be able to immediately repeal and replace Obamacare.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.320
Along with his pledge to build a wall on the
southern border

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.540
and deport illegal immigrants en masse,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:32.080
Trump's campaign was all about ramming
through the Repeal and Replace Obamacare Act,

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.060
which would have cut red tape, gotten rid
of the individual mandate

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.160
and created a true marketplace for medical insurance.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.160
Instead, thanks to the President's own lack
of savvy and GOP dithering,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.200
it didn't even get a proper vote in congress.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:45.400
Bing bing bing!

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.640
President Trump has just ordered a military
strike on Syria.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.500
The one action for which President Trump has
received bipartisan praise

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.860
was the bombing of a Syrian government airbase

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.800
to protest the alleged use of chemical weapons by the Assad regime.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.080
Even opposition leaders such as Nancy Pelosi
and Chuck Schumer

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.780
signed onto a starkly humanitarian intervention

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.880
that served no greater purpose than rallying voters here in America.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.119
Bing bing bing!

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.640
The President has issued two executive decrees

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.420
calling for a moratorium on travel from several majority Muslim countries

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:19.400
and the suspension of America's refugee program.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.140
Both have been stayed by federal courts

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.980
and it remains unclear if either will ever become the law of the land.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:30.480
We only want to admit those into our country
who will support our country.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.540
Regardless, it's anti-American to effectively
establish a religious test

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.560
for travelers and migrants here.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.540
And it also undermines attempts to reach out
to the vast majority of Muslims

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:43.780
who are the primary targets of Islamic fundamentalism.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.100
Bing bing bing!

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.480
Judge Neil Goresuch.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.800
The nomination of an intellectually powerful
and highly respected jurist

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.660
to replace the late Antonin Scalia on the supreme court

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:58.500
demonstrated that President Trump isn't the flake that many critics figured him to be.

00:01:58.509 --> 00:02:00.759
So was that a surprise? was it?

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.120
Neil Goresuch might not be Libertarian,

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:06.320
but he is in the estimation of Georgetown Law's Randy Barnett:

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.480
'a serious thinker who believes
that government power is and should be limited.'

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:12.760
Bing bing bing!

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.120
There's no question that Trump has picked
some terrible cabinet members.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.260
Attorney General Jeff Sessions has openly
talked about ramping up the war on pot

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.340
in states where it's legal, for instance.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.760
Good people don't smoke marijuana.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:27.080
He also defends asset forfeiture abuse

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.700
and has hinted at reviving federal porn prosecutions as well.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:34.560
But picks such as Ajit Pai at the Federal
Communications Commission,

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.080
Scott Gottlieb at the Food and Drug Administration

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.320
and Scott Pruitt at the Environmental Protection Agency,

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.560
are serious deregulators who are already starting
to prune back regulations

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:50.180
that accomplish little but cost taxpayers and innovators lots of time, money and resources.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:51.520
Bing bing bing!

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:55.240
Every new President enters office thinking
he can direct the course of human history

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.189
via his pen, or in the case of Trump, his twitter
feed.

00:02:58.189 --> 00:03:00.820
For all his bluster and lack of self awareness,

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:04.579
Trump is also learning that the world is more complicated than he reckoned.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.020
He's pushed back deadlines for all sorts of
projects,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.960
from funding for his stupid and useless immigration wall

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.860
to a timeline for tax reform,

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.580
which shoes that he's at least living in the real world.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:19.780
To the extent he realizes that his best path
forward is in cutting economic regulations

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.580
rather than vilifying immigrants, renegotiating
trade deals and starting new wars,

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:28.720
he'll not only be a better President, he'll create a
better America too.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.140
For Reason, I'm Nick Gillespie.

